o call a bet comfortably or see a free turn if the opponent checks back. Given the pot is small, checking is a prudent move to maximize long-term value and win probability without over-committing early against a potentially disguised hand.\n\nReason: You have a strong hand (Top Pair + Open-Ended Straight Draw) but are out of position. Checking in a limped pot conceals your strength and allows you to react to your opponent's action, while maintaining a high probability of winning at showdown or improving on later streets.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
